 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? An SSD stores data on flash memory, which pulls very little power, making it ideal for portable devices. A hard drive uses spinning disks and needs power to spin. Yes, SSDs usually save you money on bills because they don't draw power constantly. You can get small SSD for a few dollars, or a big one that beats a fast hard drive for not much more. Use an SSD for your computer, and a fast hard drive for your cloud backup. That way, if your main drive fails, you still have your photos and documents.",
